    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to satisfy the specification.\n\n**`Owner.java`**\n- Rewrote `getIdentityKey()` to return the lower-case hex **SHA-256** (64 chars) of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` \u2014 replacing the old raw `telephone|email|householdId` join. `householdId` is no longer part of identity.\n- Added a self-contained American **Soundex** implementation (`soundex(String)` + `soundexDigit(char)`) so the model has no external-dependency reliance. It's shared by the identity key and the soft-match.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Added `isDuplicateIdentity(Owner)` and wired it into `checkForConflicts` so a matching identity key now yields **409**, ignoring soft-deleted owners (via `activeOwners()`). The email-domain blocklist still runs first in `normalizeAndValidate` (400 before the conflict check).\n- Rewrote `findSoftDuplicate` to trigger when the **identityKey differs** but **soundex(lastName)** and **postcode** match \u2014 so two owners with the same surname/postcode but different telephones (hence different keys) are created as a soft match rather than rejected.\n- The separate household-duplicate 409 no longer exists; identity key is the single hard-duplicate rule. Updated the now-stale `assignHousehold` javadoc (householdId still feeds household size / membership level, just not identity).\n\n**`openapi.yml`**\n- Updated the `identityKey` field description/example to the new SHA-256 form.\n\nBehavioural effects match the spec: identical telephone/email/lastName \u21d2 same key \u21d2 409; same surname-sound + postcode but different phone \u21d2 soft match (`possibleDuplicate=true`), not rejected.",
